'' vendor/cJSON -- cJSON 1.7.19, Dave Gamble's ultralightweight JSON parser in C, as one import:
''
''     #import "vendor/cJSON" link dynamic        (or 'link static', or neither)
''
'' Every routine, type and constant of cJSON.h is then callable as cJSON documents it,
'' unqualified -- cJSON_Parse, cJSON_GetObjectItemCaseSensitive, cJSON_Print, cJSON_Delete.
'' The header is cJSON.ti, translated from cJSON.h by 'tiko c2t' and committed; its banner names
'' the C header and its SHA-256. cJSON-residue.ti holds by hand what the translation could not
'' carry: cJSON_SetIntValue, cJSON_SetNumberValue and cJSON_SetBoolValue, which are macros in C.
'' cJSON_ArrayForEach has no tiko form -- a loop header is not a macro -- so walk the children:
''
''     dim as cJSON ptr item = arr->child
''     while item
''         ...
''         item = item->next
''     wend
''
'' What cJSON_Print and its kin return is cJSON's to free: cJSON_free( text ).
''
'' cJSON_Utils.h -- JSON Pointer, JSON Patch, merge patches -- is a module of its own, as it is a
'' header of its own in C: '#import "vendor/cJSON/utils"'. It brings this one with it.
''
'' THE LIBRARY: with 'link static' cJSON is linked into the program; with 'link dynamic' -- and
'' when no '#import' says, which is this package's default -- the shared library, which tiko
'' copies beside the program: cJSON.dll, or cJSON_linux_x86_64.so on Linux.
#module "cJSON"

public #include once "cJSON.ti"
public #include once "cJSON-residue.ti"

#ifdef TIKO_LINK_STATIC
    #foreignlib CJSON static "lib/cJSON"
#else
    #foreignlib CJSON dynamic "lib/cJSON"
#endif
